  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Original 8 items plus 5 that arrived mid-session: 12 closed, 1 left open on purpose.\n\nOriginal items:\n- pt-0006 Patel, CT urogram: no cause for hematuria found; incidental 4 mm LLL nodule already followed in lung screening. First ordered a 12-month LDCT, then revised it after an outside addendum arrived (below).\n- pt-0016 Ondricka, TSH: normal, closed. Potassium: corrected from 6.3 to 4.4 (analyzer fault), normal, closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, CTA chest: item was the preliminary read. Final report: no PE and no nodule (vessel), no follow-up needed, closed. BMP: creatinine 1.64 vs 0.98 ~35 h earlier (after contrast) = AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0009), urgent patient message (avoid naproxen/NSAIDs), note.\n- pt-0064 Marchetti, 9/26 ED BMP: Cr 1.36 with no earlier creatinine in the window, so not AKI, closed.\n- pt-0033 Whitfield, 10/22 BMP: Cr 1.31; the 0.84 result was entered in error and excluded; vs 1.27 = not AKI, closed.\n- pt-0008 Brennan, K 6.4 flagged hemolyzed: urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0015) and patient message per §2. This changed after a correction (below).\n\nArrivals (RBC-INBOX-01 §8):\n- pt-0008: lab corrected that the specimen was NOT hemolyzed. Switched to RBC-LAB-03 §1: stat BMP today (sr-t0019, replaces sr-t0015), pool-oncall notified stat, corrected patient message to come in today, meds reviewed (no K-raising drug safely holdable; metoprolol kept), note.\n- pt-0033: new outside Cr 1.78 vs 1.31 the same morning = AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0024), patient messaged, note.\n- pt-0064: new outside Cr 1.48 vs 0.88 ~35 h earlier = AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0025), patient messaged, note. The 9/26 decision stands.\n- pt-0006: Lakeshore addendum revised the 4/14 LDCT to Lung-RADS 3 (new 5 mm RUL nodule), LDCT in 6 months. Ordered LDCT for 10/23–11/14 (sr-t0032), tracking task due 11/14 (task-t0033), corrected patient message, note. I can't cancel orders, so task-t0034 asks you to discontinue the superseded 12-month LDCT order sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002.\n\nLeft open:\n- inbox-a0002 (pt-0007 chest X-ray): preliminary only, possible 7 mm RUL opacity. No final report yet, so left open per §2(c).\n\nNot touched: the 6 refill requests in your messages queue. They were there before I started and aren't part of the results inbox.",
